cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MolecuLens in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MolecuLens（分子视镜）"
abstract: >-
  MolecuLens is a local, single-window molecular viewer and rendering engine for
  structural biology and computational chemistry. It reads PDB, GRO, SDF and
  Gaussian cube files plus DCD, XTC and TRR trajectories, draws them in a real-time
  Vulkan viewport with 17 representations and 23 material presets, maps electrostatic
  potential onto isosurfaces, and exports publication figures through a built-in CPU
  ray tracer. Every visible setting has a matching command-line flag, so a figure
  tuned interactively can be reproduced bit-for-bit from a script.
authors:
  - family-names: "moyuMaster"
    alias: "moyuMaster"
repository-code: "https://github.com/moyudoing/MolecuLens"
url: "https://moyudoing.github.io/MolecuLens/"
license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "2.13.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
keywords:
  - "molecular visualization"
  - "molecular graphics"
  - "structural biology"
  - "computational chemistry"
  - "Vulkan"
  - "ray tracing"
  - "trajectory analysis"
  - "electrostatic potential"
  - "publication figures"
  - "C++20"
